  "title": "Fix spelling and grammar in player hints",
  "description": "Superseded by the GitHub review: https://github.com/LuminariMUD/Luminari-Source/pull/234\n\nThe rotating player hints contained misspellings, repeated words, broken sentence structure, and missing spaces between adjacent C strings. Audit all 96 hints and correct 64 entries plus the hint-toggle message, including the clan hint's \"communcation\" and repeated \"There there\".\n\nPreserve gameplay details, hint order and count, color codes, opt-out footers, URLs, and hint-selection logic. The change is limited to player-facing strings in `src/act/act.other.c`.\n\nValidation:\n- `pre-commit run --files src/act/act.other.c` and the installed commit/push hooks passed.\n- The pre-push `Verify build compiles` hook passed.\n- `make -j2 src/act/act.other.o` compiled without warnings.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Checked all assembled hint strings and verified all 96 entries retain their numbering/order, control sequences, footers, and URLs; executable logic is unchanged.\n\nThe full test suite and a live-game smoke test were not run for this text-only change. No production deployment was performed.",
